.\" Man page for atlas project command
.\" Updated: July 2026
.TH PROJECT 1 "July 2026" "atlas 0.13.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
atlas\-project \- project registry operations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B atlas project
\fIcommand\fR [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B atlas project
manages the project registry. Projects are discovered by scanning directories
for marker files (package.json, DESCRIPTION, etc.) or registered manually.
.PP
The registry is stored in \fI~/.atlas/projects.json\fR (filesystem) or
\fI~/.atlas/atlas.db\fR (SQLite).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBadd\fR [\fIpath\fR]
Register a project. If no path is given, uses current directory.
.RS
Options:
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tags\fR \fItags\fR
Comma\-separated tags for the project.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-status\fR \fIstatus\fR
Initial status: active, paused, archived (default: active).
.RE
.TP
\fBlist\fR
List all registered projects.
.RS
Options:
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-status\fR \fIstatus\fR
Filter by status: active, paused, blocked, archived, complete.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tag\fR \fItag\fR
Filter by tag.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fIformat\fR
Output format: table, json, names (default: table).
.TP
\fB\-\-count\fR
Show project count only.
.TP
\fB\-\-suggest\fR
Suggest project for input (fuzzy match).
.RE
.TP
\fBshow\fR \fIname\fR
Show detailed information for a project.
.RS
Options:
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output as JSON.
.RE
.TP
\fBremove\fR \fIname\fR
Unregister a project from the registry.
.SH EXAMPLES
Register current directory:
.RS
.nf
atlas project add
.fi
.RE
.PP
Register with tags:
.RS
.nf
atlas project add ~/projects/myapp \-\-tags "web,node"
.fi
.RE
.PP
List active projects:
.RS
.nf
atlas project list \-\-status active
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show project as JSON:
.RS
.nf
atlas project show atlas \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Remove a project:
.RS
.nf
atlas project remove old\-project
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.atlas/projects.json
Project registry (filesystem backend).
.TP
.I ~/.atlas/atlas.db
Project registry (SQLite backend).
